---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import EnvChecker from '../../components/EnvChecker.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Environment Variable Checker"
  description="Compare your required environment variables against what's actually set — catch missing config before you deploy."
>
  <EnvChecker client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Catch missing config before deployment fails</h2>
  <p>
    "It works on my machine" often means a required environment variable
    exists locally but wasn't set in staging or production. This tool
    compares your list of required variables against what you've actually
    provided, flagging what's missing before you find out the hard way.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use this</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>List the variables your app requires, one per line.</li>
    <li>Paste your actual .env content (or just a list of keys).</li>
    <li>Review what's missing, matched, and extra/unused.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Environment Variable Checker FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Does this check values, or just key names?</strong> Just key
    presence — it doesn't validate that values are correct, only that the
    variable exists.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Is my data sent anywhere?</strong> No — comparison happens
    entirely in your browser.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
